Diamond Cutter Translation Tool
Copyright (c) 2026 Asian Legacy Library (ALL) / Asian Classics Input
Project (ACIP). All rights reserved.

STATUS OF THIS FILE
-------------------
Added 2026-08-23 because the project had no licence file at all, which
an SQA audit named as a gap (BUILD-2). It states ONLY what this
repository already records, with the date and the place each statement
comes from. Adam read and accepted it on 2026-08-23; it has NOT been
reviewed by counsel. Nothing in it grants anyone a licence; where a
question is open, it says so instead of answering it.


1. THE SOFTWARE
---------------
The application source in this repository — app/, core/, ocr/, tools/ —
is the Asian Legacy Library's own work. No public licence is granted
for it here. Copies are given to named recipients (translators, the
monastic input centres, students of the tradition) as builds, not as
source.

Distribution stance of record: "The Diamond Cutter Translation Tool is
distributed FREE OF CHARGE and is not sold." — Adam's ruling,
2026-08-22, recorded in docs/SHIP.md. That ruling is what places the
bundled CC BY-NC recognition models inside their licence; if the stance
ever changes, that bundling has to be revisited before anything else.


2. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE IN THE APPLICATION
------------------------------------------
The application bundles ~33 upstream open-source projects, including
Qt 6 (LGPL-3.0-only), GLib (LGPL-2.1-or-later) and the GCC runtime
libraries (GPL-3.0-or-later WITH the GCC Runtime Library Exception).
Their terms are not this project's to set, and this file does not
override them.

  * Prose list, per component:  docs/distribution/OPEN_SOURCE_NOTICES.md
  * Generated, per binary:      inside each build, at
      "…app/Contents/Resources/licenses/BUNDLED_COMPONENTS.tsv"
    beside the licence texts themselves.

The LGPL libraries are used unmodified and dynamically linked; they can
be replaced in the bundle. See the LGPL notice in OPEN_SOURCE_NOTICES.md
for how, and for which licence texts a given build was able to ship.


3. THE DATA
-----------
The Geshe Michael Roach Dictionary, the aligned corpus, the registers
and the published apparatus are the Asian Legacy Library's own data,
(c) their respective authors, distributed within the ALL/ACIP team.
Geshe Michael Roach's English is the binding layer of that data;
nothing here relicenses or republishes it.

Reference layers carry their own terms, one per row, in
docs/distribution/OPEN_SOURCE_NOTICES.md and
docs/distribution/PAYLOAD_MANIFEST.txt. Two things follow that are
easy to get wrong, so they are stated plainly:

  * A DMG pressed in TEAM mode contains build/reference.db —
    unlicensed third-party dictionary compilations kept for in-house
    lookup. A team DMG must not be forwarded outside the ALL/ACIP
    team. Its own README.txt says so.
  * Several layers ship under terms that are recorded as OPEN, not
    settled: the redistribution stance for the HGM release package,
    the teachings-index consent line, the SOAS POS terms, and the
    per-file terms for 20 files under data/extracted. They are
    itemised in PAYLOAD_MANIFEST.txt with status `gated` or `itemise`,
    and a market-mode press refuses to build while they stand.


4. TRADEMARKS AND NAMES
-----------------------
"Asian Legacy Library", "Asian Classics Input Project", "Diamond Cutter"
and the names of the teachers and organisations referenced in the data
are used with those organisations' own authorisation and are not
licensed by this file.


5. NO WARRANTY
--------------
The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
or implied. The tool's machine-produced output — segmentations,
auto-aligned glosses, OCR, phonetics — is review material and is
labelled as such in the interface. It is not a substitute for a
translator's judgement.


Corrections: if you are the author of a component or layer named in
OPEN_SOURCE_NOTICES.md and want the attribution changed, contact the
Asian Legacy Library and it will be changed in the next release.
